# Git Commit Rules

## Author Identity

All commits MUST use the following identity:

- **Name**: `Karmagate`
- **Email**: `dennis@karmagate.com`

When creating or amending commits, ALWAYS set environment variables:

```bash
GIT_AUTHOR_NAME="Karmagate"
GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL="dennis@karmagate.com"
GIT_COMMITTER_NAME="Karmagate"
GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL="dennis@karmagate.com"
```

## No AI Co-Author Trailers

NEVER allow `Co-authored-by` trailers in commit messages. Cursor automatically appends `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>` — this must be prevented.

To avoid it, always use `--no-verify` flag and pass commit message explicitly:

```bash
GIT_AUTHOR_NAME="Karmagate" GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL="dennis@karmagate.com" \
GIT_COMMITTER_NAME="Karmagate" GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL="dennis@karmagate.com" \
git -c commit.gpgsign=false commit --no-verify -m 'commit message'
```

## Rules Summary

1. Author and committer must always be `Karmagate <dennis@karmagate.com>`
2. No `Co-authored-by` lines in commit messages
3. No mentions of Cursor, Claude, or any AI tools in commits
4. Always verify commit message is clean after creating it
